<PageTitle>Gantt chart — FlexCore Showcase</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Gantt chart" Category="Charts" CategoryHref="demo/charts" ControlName="GanttControl"
                   Tagline="A task list with a timeline: hierarchy, dependencies, progress, and editing by dialog or by dragging the bars."
                   SourcePath="Gantt/GanttControl.razor;Gantt/GanttModels.cs">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            <code>GanttControl</code> is a <code>TreeGridControl</code> whose last column draws each task as a bar on a day-scaled timeline.
            Tasks are plain <code>GanttTask</code> objects: a title, start and end, a progress percentage, an optional parent (the row nests
            under it) and a comma-separated list of predecessor ids (drawn as arrows). The toolbar adds, edits and deletes tasks through a
            dialog, expands or collapses the tree, and switches the timescale. A bar can be dragged to move its task and either end dragged
            to resize it. Every change is validated and offered to <code>TaskChanging</code> before <code>TasksChanged</code> delivers the
            new list. The control never edits the objects it was given: it works on clones and hands back clones.
        </p>
        <p>
            The timeline runs from the earliest start to two days after the latest end and is at least 14 days wide. One day is 72, 32, 8
            or 2 pixels in the Day, Week, Month and Year views; drags snap to whole days and keep each task's time of day.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="schedule" Title="Project schedule" RazorCode="@Code.Schedule" CSharpCode="@Code.ScheduleCs">
            <Description><p>Nine tasks in two phases with dependencies between them. Add opens the dialog for a new task; select a row and Edit or Delete act on it, as does a double-click on the row. Drag a bar to move its task, drag either end to change its length, or put the focus on an end handle and press the arrow keys. A change that breaks a rule (an end before its start, a task starting before a predecessor finishes, a delete while other tasks still point at the task) is refused with a message under the toolbar. The line under the chart is built from the list <code>TasksChanged</code> delivers.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <GanttControl Tasks="@_tasks" TasksChanged="t => _tasks = t" Height="380px" />
                <p class="result">@Summary</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="views" Title="Read-only timeline with a task template" RazorCode="@Code.Views" CSharpCode="@Code.ViewsCs">
            <Description><p>The same plan with <code>AllowEditing</code> off: Add, Edit and Delete are disabled, the dialog and the drag handles are gone, while Expand all, Collapse all and the timescale still work. The Task column uses <code>TaskTemplate</code> to add the progress figure. <code>View</code> is bound both ways: the buttons set it from the page and the toolbar's dropdown reports back through <code>ViewChanged</code>.</p></Description>
            <Controls>
                @foreach (var v in Enum.GetValues<GanttView>())
                {
                    <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" Disabled="@(_view == v)" OnClick="() => _view = v">@v</ButtonControl>
                }
            </Controls>
            <Demo>
                <GanttControl Tasks="@_plan" AllowEditing="false" View="@_view" ViewChanged="v => _view = v" Height="380px">
                    <TaskTemplate Context="task">
                        <span>@task.Title</span> <span class="pct">@task.Progress%</span>
                    </TaskTemplate>
                </GanttControl>
                <p class="result">View: @_view.</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="veto" Title="Vetoing a change" RazorCode="@Code.Veto" CSharpCode="@Code.VetoCs">
            <Description><p><code>TaskChanging</code> sees every create, update and delete after the control's own validation has passed, with the action, the proposed task and the stored one. Here finished tasks are locked and nothing can be deleted: drag the Wireframes bar a day to the left, or select Launch and press Delete, and the guard refuses. The control shows no message for a refusal (a refused drag snaps back, a refused delete closes its prompt, a refused edit leaves the dialog open), so the line under the chart reports the decision. A delete of a task that others still depend on, Wireframes for one, never reaches the guard: the control's own rule refuses it first with its message under the toolbar.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <GanttControl Tasks="@_guarded" TasksChanged="t => _guarded = t" TaskChanging="Guard" Height="380px" />
                <p class="result">@_decision</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="GanttControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Params" />
        <p>
            <code>CssClass</code>, <code>Style</code>, <code>Id</code>, <code>Visible</code>, <code>Enabled</code> and
            <code>AdditionalAttributes</code> come from <code>FlexControlBase</code> and apply to the root <code>div</code>;
            <code>Enabled="false"</code> disables editing the same way <code>AllowEditing</code> does.
        </p>
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Events" Title="GanttControl events" Rows="Vocab.Events" />
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Methods" Title="GanttControl methods" Rows="Vocab.Methods" />
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="GanttControl read-only state" Rows="Vocab.State" />
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="GanttTask" Rows="Vocab.Task" />
        <p>
            <code>GanttTask.Clone()</code> returns a shallow copy; the control uses it for everything it stores and everything it hands back.
            <code>GanttView</code> is <code>Day</code>, <code>Week</code>, <code>Month</code> or <code>Year</code>;
            <code>GanttChangeAction</code> is <code>Create</code>, <code>Update</code> or <code>Delete</code>.
        </p>
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="GanttTaskChangingArgs" Rows="Vocab.Args" />
        <p>Rules a schedule has to pass. The incoming <code>Tasks</code> list is checked against all of them except the dependency rule; every change is checked against all of them for the whole schedule.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Ids are unique and not empty.</li>
            <li><code>End</code> is not before <code>Start</code>.</li>
            <li><code>Title</code> has at least one character and <code>Progress</code> is 0 to 100 (data annotations on <code>GanttTask</code>).</li>
            <li><code>ParentId</code> and every id in <code>Predecessors</code> name an existing task.</li>
            <li>With <code>EnforceDependencies</code>, each predecessor ends on or before the task starts.</li>
            <li>Neither the parent chain nor the dependency graph contains a cycle.</li>
            <li>A task is not deleted while another task names it as parent or predecessor.</li>
        </ul>
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Keyboard" Title="Keyboard" Rows="Vocab.Keys" />
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssClasses" Title="CSS classes" Rows="Vocab.Css" />
    </Vocabulary>

    <Accessibility>
        <p>
            Each bar is a button labelled "Edit <em>title</em>" and each end handle "Resize start of <em>title</em>" or "Resize end of
            <em>title</em>", so they are reachable with Tab. The validation message has <code>role="alert"</code>. The timescale dropdown
            is labelled "Gantt timescale". The dependency arrows are SVG hidden from assistive technology; the relation itself is in the
            task's Predecessor tasks field in the editor.
        </p>
    </Accessibility>

    <Related>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="demo/charts">Charts overview</a>: <code>ChartControl</code> also has a Gantt chart type, a static timeline drawn from chart series without rows, editing or dependencies.</li>
            <li><a href="demo/grid/tree-grid">Tree grid</a>: the hierarchical grid the task list is built on.</li>
        </ul>
    </Related>
</FeatureDemoLayout>

